Forward+ Renderer\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a SpinBox's value is programmatically set to its min_value or max_value, the corresponding up/down arrow button should visually update to its disabled style.\n\nThis works correctly when using the set_value() method.\n\nHowever, when using the set_value_no_signal() method, the internal value of the SpinBox is updated correctly, but the GUI does not refresh the disabled state of the arrow buttons. For example, if the value is set to max_value via set_value_no_signal(), the up-arrow remains visually enabled, even though it cannot be clicked to increase the value further.\n\nThe expected behavior is that set_value_no_signal() should update the internal value and the node's own visual state, while only skipping the emission of the value_changed signal.\n\n```gdscript\nextends Control\n\n@onready var spin_box: SpinBox = $SpinBox\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n\tspin_box.set_value_no_signal(100)\n```\n\n<img width=\"745\" height=\"362\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/389466a5-b2e4-4fa2-be98-95fef885765b\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new scene with a Control node as the root.\n2. Add a SpinBox node. Set its max_value to 100.\n4. Attach the following GDScript to the root Control node.\n5. Run the scene.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.